			"notes": "- Server settings can be listed and changed from the server console and over RCON with /pandorical settings, so a server's choices can be scripted.\n- Chat shows the sender's face beside each message a player sends: a client setting, on unless you turn it off, left to Chat Heads when it is installed.\n- The mods screen has a search box, shows your own mods' icons, and opens each mod's readme with its licence, contributors, the mods bundled inside it, and links: homepage, issues, source and any it gave Mod Menu. A link asks before it opens.\n- A Mods folder button opens your own mods folder.\n- The Mods button also works on the title screen and on servers without Pandorical, opening your game's own list of mods, unless Mod Menu is installed.\n- A mod that declared a config screen for Mod Menu gets a Configure button on either mods screen, with or without Mod Menu installed.\n- Mod Menu is listed as overlapping Pandorical, so the game notes it at startup; the two still run side by side.\n- The mods screen lists up to 256 of your own mods, not 64. In a very large pack, some are listed without their readmes."
		},
